						<p class="pDate">Thursday, March 31, 2005</p>
						<p class="pTitle">guidefox.com - EverQuest Guides </p>
							<p class=pText>
							An online shop for professional guides for EverQuest and other popular MMORPGs.<br><br><a href ="http://www.guidefox.com/eq/everquest-guides.htm" target="_TOP">www.guidefox.com</a><BR><br><br>I've check out a couple of these guides they're quite informative and have a good layout. If your looking for some additional information about your favorite MMORPG it's definately worth a look.<br>
							<br>
							 - Ganza<BR><BR>
							</p>
							
					
						<p class="pDate">Saturday, March 26, 2005</p>
						<p class="pTitle">The BB/Sol Ro Merge </p>
							<p class=pText>
							<p style="text-indent: 10; line-height: 150%; word-spacing: 0; margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 5" align="justify"><font face="Comic Sans MS">An end of an Era has happened.  Sol Ro is no more.  It closed its doors and waved sadly goodbye to everyone Wednesday and showed them the road to Bristlebane.</font></p><br><p style="text-indent: 10; line-height: 150%; word-spacing: 0; margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 5" align="justify"><font face="Comic Sans MS">For those of you that still come here and before Ganza says goodbye to the website, I wanted to give Sol Ro the link to the BB Forums.</font></p><br><p style="text-indent: 10; line-height: 150%; word-spacing: 0; margin-top: 0" align="center"><a href="http://bristlebane.org/v-web/bulletin/bb/index.php?sid=95e0f8915a4ad57103cec523f111be44"><b><font face="Comic Sans MS" size="4">BRISTLEBANE FORUMS</font></b></a></p><br><p style="text-indent: 10; line-height: 150%; word-spacing: 0; margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 5" align="justify"><font face="Comic Sans MS">I am hearing much negativity coming from the old players of BB for us coming to them.  Well, you know what?  It needed to be done.  Things will be nuts for a while, but hang in there and let the fire die down from the move.  They need to get to know us and us them.  I played on BB for a little bit on and off for the past 2 years.  Got to know a few people and they were all nice, helpful, and fun people.  Show them we are better than the ones that are making rude comments.  Show them <b>WHY</b> our <b> SERVER</b> was <b>GREAT</b>!  And when all else fails?  (For those of you that have heard and know the joke):</font></p><br><p style="line-height: 150%; word-spacing: 0; margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 5" align="center"><font face="Comic Sans MS" color="#FF0000" size="2"><b>ADRA DID IT!</b></font></p><br><p style="line-height: 150%; word-spacing: 0; margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 5" align="center"><font face="Comic Sans MS" color="#FF0000" size="2"><b>BLAME ADRA</b></font></p><br><p style="line-height: 150%; word-spacing: 0; margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 5" align="center"><font face="Comic Sans MS" color="#FF0000" size="2"><b>IT'S ADRA'S FAULT</b></font></p><br><p style="text-indent: 10; line-height: 150%; word-spacing: 0; margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 5" align="justify"><font face="Comic Sans MS">Now go HAVE FUN!</font></p><br><p style="line-height: 150%; word-spacing: 0; margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 5" align="center"> </p><br><p style="line-height: 150%; word-spacing: 0; margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 5" align="center"><font face="Comic Sans MS">Adra, formerly of Sol Ro, now of Whisperwind (WoW) MUHAHAHA  (Ya and look for me every now and again on BB, too!)</font></p>
							<br>
							 - Adrastea<BR><BR>
							</p>
							
					
						<p class="pDate">Sunday, February 27, 2005</p>
						<p class="pTitle">Ending of Solusekro and a Guild... </p>
							<p class=pText>
							The once great guild of Stone Circle will be disbanding and moving on to other things. We would like to thank all of Norrath for the fun and time we have shared together. So the name of Stone Circle shall be but a memory in the heart and soul of all Norrathians good luck to all and my your friends be many and your swords be sharp...<br><br>~Warna
							<br>
							 - Warna<BR><BR>
							</p>
							&nbsp;<a class="abody" href="comments.asp?Index=600">[View Comments]</a>
					
					
						<p class="pDate">Friday, February 25, 2005</p>
						<p class="pTitle">The Entire Story...  </p>
							<p class=pText>
							I know Ganza gave the link, but sometimes this site just does not want to load for me and a few others I know....<br><br><br><br>Server Merges<br>On March 22, 2005, we will begin the process of merging some of the EverQuest servers.  As we have seen from the recent success of the Zek merger, combining some of the EQ worlds is beneficial for players’ experience.  In fact, we have been pleasantly surprised to find that the new Zek server now has a higher population than the four combined servers had prior to that merger.  We hope that by merging some of our lower population servers with a higher population server, we will continue to enhance your gameplay experience<br><br>Merging Servers<br><br>On March 22nd, Antonius Bayle will merge with Kane Bayle and will retain the name Antonius Bayle. <br><br>On March 23rd, Bristlebane will merge with Solusek Ro and will retain the name Bristlebane.  <br><br>We understand that server identity is important to our customers and we will be integrating server titles into the title system to allow you to display your server of origin, should you desire to do so.  <br><br>Unutilized Character Purge<br><br>Immediately preceding the merger, all characters below level 10 that have not been logged in for over six months will be deleted from each of the merging servers and will not be available after the server merge.  If you have a character on any of the servers being merged that is below level 10 and has not been logged in for more than six months, you will need to log that character in prior to the scheduled merge date for the relevant server.  <br><br>Shared Banks on Merging Servers<br><br>If you have characters on two servers which are being merged together, you will need to clean out the shared bank on one of those servers. After the merge, only one shared bank will be available on each merged server.<br><br>Character Limitations<br><br>If you have more than eight characters in total on two servers being merged together, only the first eight characters (in alphabetical order) will be displayed after the merge.  Characters other than the eight displayed characters will not be available for selection until currently displayed characters are deleted.  All characters from both servers will remain on your account provided that the character was not below level 10 and had not been logged in within the last six months.<br><br>Corpses<br><br>Prior to the scheduled merge date for your server(s), please be sure that you clear any unclaimed character corpses from the world.  Character corpses will not be transferred to the newly-merged server.  Once the merger is complete, all corpses on the servers affected by a merge will have been purged.<br><br>Duplicate Character Names<br><br>It is possible that characters on servers affected by the merge will have duplicate names. In the event that characters on the new, combined server do share a name, the character with the most played time will be entitled to keep the name. All other characters will have the letter X appended to their name and will be eligible for a name change.  Characters can use the in-game /changename command to request a new name.  The new name is subject to the conditions set forth in our naming policy which can be found here: Naming Policy.<br><br>LDoN Leader Boards<br><br>After each merge is completed, as characters log into their newly-combined server, the leader board will be re-populated with standings. Although your points will be unaffected by the transfer, your standing may have changed based on the new, combined population totals.<br><br>Complimentary Character Move<br><br>Shortly after each merger is complete, we will allow all customers affected by a merge a one-time, complimentary character move to the server of their choice.  For each customer with an account on a newly-merged server who request such a move, all characters associated with that customer’s account will be transferred to the selected server.  All characters will bring their items with them in the transfer.<br><br>Brenlo Bixiebopper<br>Community Relations Manager<br><br>---------------------------------------------<br>Halfling, Cajun Style! <br><br><br>http://eqforums.station.sony.com/eq/board/message?board.id=Crier&message.id=84&no_redir=true
							<br>
							 - Adrastea<BR><BR>
							</p>
							&nbsp;<a class="abody" href="comments.asp?Index=599">[View Comments]</a>
					
					
						<p class="pDate">Thursday, February 24, 2005</p>
						<p class="pTitle">Solusek Ro Server merging to Bristlebane </p>
							<p class=pText>
							News from Sony Online Entertainment <br><br>Merging Servers<br><br>On March 22nd, Antonius Bayle will merge with Kane Bayle and will retain the name Antonius Bayle. <br><br>On March 23rd, Bristlebane will merge with Solusek Ro and will retain the name Bristlebane.  <br><br>We understand that server identity is important to our customers and we will be integrating server titles into the title system to allow you to display your server of origin, should you desire to do so.<br><br>For complete news visit: <a href="http://eqlive.station.sony.com/community/dev_view.jsp?id=64026" target=_TOP>http://eqlive.station.sony.com/community/dev_view.jsp?id=64026</a><br><br>After the server merger solusekro.com will be no more. If anyone happens to be interested in the domain name shoot me an email at ganza@solusekro.com<br><br>Solusek Ro, the greatest server in Everquest shall be missed<br><br>
							<br>
							 - Ganza<BR><BR>
							</p>
							&nbsp;<a class="abody" href="comments.asp?Index=598">[View Comments]</a>
					
					
						<p class="pDate">Thursday, February 17, 2005</p>
						<p class="pTitle">Guild In Search of Leaders </p>
							<p class=pText>
							Are you a former officer or leader of a guild that just could not make it through the EQ2/WoW releases? We would like to offer those people looking for a guild with excellent leading ability the chance to prove it. We have recently had some positions open within the Solusek Ro Branch that need to be filled by self driven leader like characters. Visit our home page ar www.warriors-caste.org if it looks like something you would be interested in and you feel you can work within our rule set send me a message through the website. We would be glad to give you the chance.<br>Tubzinsac Greywanderer<br>Leader of the Warriors' Caste
							<br>
							 - Tubzinsac<BR><BR>
							</p>
							
					
						<p class="pDate">Monday, February 07, 2005</p>
						<p class="pTitle">Recruitment Update </p>
							<p class=pText>
							<Lords of Prophecy> looking for active players who love to raid and want to progress with us through PoP. Check requirements and current news at<br>http://www.vytco.com<br> Tuesday, Feb 08, 2005 we starting 1 full round of backflags to EPs. APPLY TODAY!
							<br>
							 - Flaor<BR><BR>
							</p>
							
					
						<p class="pDate">Friday, February 04, 2005</p>
						<p class="pTitle">Serra Advocates </p>
							<p class=pText>
							Serra Advocates now has a new Website:<br>http://serraadvocates.guildwizard.com/<br><br>(old site was http://www.serraadvocates.com/)
							<br>
							 - Rydan<BR><BR>
							</p>
							
					
						<p class="pDate">Thursday, December 30, 2004</p>
						<p class="pTitle">The Time Has Come... </p>
							<p class=pText>
							As Selias has already stated, SH will become a Myth in the winds of Norrath.  However, we have moved on to WoW, Whisperwind Server in the form of the "Mythfits".<br><br>Over the past 3 years we have watched several young ones grow up, spread their wings and move on to Raiding Guilds such as DB, Triadica, Empy and others.  Unlike other Guilds that have handed the reins to another, we decided to just disband SH and let our people move forth to new aspirations and lands.  We will pop up from time to time, so don't think you have gotten rid or Sunny & Ecc or Selias & Adra.<br><br>We will miss many and will hope to cross paths again in the future of the gaming world.  Always feel welcome to come say Hi and watch the metamorphis of changes to the SH Site over the next several days!<br><br>Adrastea - Sacred Honor Retired Guild Liaison<br>Adra - Mythfits - Head Mythtress
							<br>
							 - Adrastea<BR><BR>
							</p>
							&nbsp;<a class="abody" href="comments.asp?Index=593">[View Comments]</a>
					
<center>
<img src=images/redline.gif height=1 width=100%>				
</center>
					

						<p class="pTitle">Sacred Honor Disbanding </p>
							<p class=pText>
							Sacred Honor Guild will be disbanding as of the end of 2004. We regret that the guildname will no longer be seen around Norrath on Solusek Ro but feel retiring the good name of Sacred Honor preferential to handing it off to another like a hand-me-down article of clothing. Sacred Honor maintained a good reputation with the majority of Norrath and succeeded in accomplishing a great many things, not only for it's members but also for allies, friends and relative strangers within the realm of Norrath. <BR>Caio!<BR>Selias Trailtracker<BR>(guildleader of Sacred Honor)
							<br>
							 - Selias Trailtracker<BR><BR>
							</p>
							
					
						<p class="pDate">Friday, December 17, 2004</p>
						<p class="pTitle">Mystic Crusaders Looking for New Recruits. </p>
							<p class=pText>
							Mystic Crusaders are looking for a few good adventures to fill the slots of those that have journeyed on to WoW and EQ2.  If you are looking for a wild bunch of peeps with a great sense of humor and a willingness to go just about anywheres on norrath you should make it a point to check us out.  http://www.mysticcrusaders.org/main.htm<br>Check us out or find one of us in game we'd be more than glad to help ya out.  -Anjilkins
							<br>
							 - Aengel<BR><BR>
							</p>
							
					
						<p class="pDate">Wednesday, December 15, 2004</p>
						<p class="pTitle">Lords of Prophecy </p>
							<p class=pText>
							"Lords of Prophecy" is looking for motivated and fun people who play during US evening times. We are L65+ raiding family with "no-drama" policy. <br><br>Visit us at www.VYTCO.com or tell in game to Krushor, Berrywine or Flaor for more info.
							<br>
							 - Flaor McLife<BR><BR>
							</p>
							
<center>
<img src=images/redline.gif height=1 width=100%>				
</center>
					

						<p class="pTitle">Grats to Eye of Mordor/Corona Mundi! </p>
