						<p class="pDate">Thursday, November 30, 2000</p>
						<p class="pTitle">RPGwear new design - Clarity </p>
							<p class=pText>
							<b> Battle survival Pill new target against slow mana regeneration</b><br><br><p>Norrath, Nov 29 (<a href="http://www.rpgwear.com" target="_blank">www.rpgwear.com</a>) - Speeding the<br><br>action of a gene that helps mana regenerate on less oxygen could<br><br>provide a new strategy for fighting baddies, researchers report. </p><br><br><p>Dr. RPGwear and colleagues at the RPG Inc<br><br>Institute in Freeport, Norrath have designed a pill that speeds up<br><br>the pathway by which this gene, CLARITY, initiates a series of<br><br>events that allow mana cells to regenerate in low-oxygen<br><br>conditions faster. This pill speeds up the growth of mana in<br><br>various casters throughout the land, according to the test reports<br><br>done on plague rats in Befallen. </p><br><br><p>"These findings raise the exciting<br><br>possibility of a new approach to faster mana regeneration with a<br><br>pill, though a number of issues will require careful consideration<br><br>in developing such a strategy," Dr. Feelgood and colleagues<br><br>from the Fay Trust Centre for Enchanter Genetics in Felwithe,<br><br>Faydwer. </p><br><br><p><br><br><br>Prescriptions are available under the counter at<br><br>your local EQ Pharmacy located at <a href="http://www.RPGwear.com">www.RPGwear.com</a>.</p>
							<br>
							 - Xar<BR><BR>
							</p>
							
					
