						<p class="pTitle">Here It Is!!! </p>
							<p class=pText>
							Well here it is, all the info you need about VP from FoH WWW:<br><br><BR>Important: Once you zone in, the only way out is 1. Death, or 2. Through at VERY LEAST 3 dragons that make nagafen look like a froglok shin knight. <BR><br><br><BR>Right when you zone into VP's, group up to the left of the entry point. It's about the only safe spot in the zone. Take your time and group up and prep here. When you move from here, there really isn't turning back, unless you die. <BR><br><br><BR>At the safe zone in point, I'd highly recommend a shaman using Vision to follow the wurm's around. Learn the pathing patterns and timing of the wurms and ESPECIALLY the named Dragons. The two of Primary concern are SilverWing as previously mentioned, and Hoskar, who's the meaner of the two. <BR><br><br><BR>Your absolute worst nightmare is having to fight the two dragons at once, so make absolutelyu sure, when you fight one, the other one is far away. <BR><br><br><BR>As previously stated, the mobs here spawn almost instaneously. Wurm die, wurm pop. <BR>The dragons however do take a long spawn cycle, and have very very good loot. <BR><br><br><BR>The optimal attack plan we found, was to tackle the 1st wurm as he come across the bridge toward the entry point. <BR><br><br><BR>Then walk dead center past the 2 raptors. They have low aggro radiuses, so don't waste time fighting them, cause if you do, the prevuiyd wurm will be quickly upon you. <BR><br><br><BR>This corridor and the subsquent large ramp heading up is the optimal place to fight your 1st dragon. Whether it be Silverwing or Hoskar. <BR><br><BR>Hopefully at this point you have a dedicated shaman trailing one of the dragons with vision. You need to know where they are!!!! <BR><br><br><BR>Once you kill one of the dragons, I'd recommend holding your ground kill the inc wurms, and ambush the other dragon on his way to you. <BR><br><br><BR>At this point, you can move up the ramp and past the bridge. If you head straight, it splits, to the left is a safe area, with no spawns or mobs. This is a FANTASTIC place to keep a cleric or something logged here permanently. Cause in future runs in VP, if you can drag corpses to here for res'ing, and regroup here, it's far far simpler to pull the dragons solo to this point to pulverize. So... utilize this point so your 2nd trip and beyond to VP are easier. <BR><br><br><BR>Ok to proceed further. Remeber that bridge after the ramp. Instead of heading straight and left to the safe point. Follow the right ledge RIGHT after the bridge further up. <BR><br><br><BR>You will encounter a few more Wurms, which should be cake walk for you now. <BR><br><br><BR>The next room should be 6 raptors guarding a room with a few statues. The raptors can probably be pulled solo, or at no more than 3 at a time. They aren't that hard. <BR><br><br><BR>You will mosey on further, usual stuff, until a setup of 2 raps+2drakes, and maybe 2 wandering wurms. This ought to be a tricky fight, but easire than the dragons. <BR><br><br><BR>Note: Might be worth tryinng some enchanter tricks on the raptors, I believe they were charmable at a certain point, but might've been changed. Definitely worth charming one of them beasts to help you out. <BR><br><br><BR>If I remeber correctly, silverwing+hoskar are the only wandering "dragon"s in VP. The others are all behind giant double doors. <BR><br><br><BR>The Dragon that guards the portal out, Nexar? blue guy, Breathes nasty Acid attack, and is also guarded by a blue drake, and possible wandering wurm. not an easy fight. <BR><br><br><BR>There are a few more dragons in there, but the toughest mofo of them all is called Phara Dar. <BR>He is black+purple with kinda unicorn type of horns. But more importantly, he has an AoE mez. I remeber fighting him, and having the entire group mez'd stunned. oh he had a 800-1200 dmg too. I think out of 30 or so people, only one person actually got through his stun and landed a few hits on him. <BR><br><br><BR>I'll have the plane of sky breakdown and all the tricks when I can find more words to fit Brad+Buttchump butler. <BR><br><br><BR>I post this with a HEARTY middle finger up Butler + Brad's Shared Ass. And any copy/reproduction of this note, please include this part. <BR><br><br><BR>I guess those beta-testers from the test server are just a tad bit pissed off still =P<BR><br><br>This is from a post on the message board.<BR><BR><BR><BR><BR>
							<br>
							 - Anumatu<BR><BR>
							</p>
							
<center>
<img src=images/redline.gif height=1 width=100%>				
</center>
					

						<p class="pTitle">The Hole Now Open! </p>
							<p class=pText>
							***Today's Updates***<BR><BR><BR>*The Hole*<BR><BR><BR>We are pleased to announce the opening of The Hole, a high-level dungeon on the continent of Odus.  The Hole is a complementary addition to EverQuest, available to all subscribers regardless of their Kunark status.  The files necessary to enter The Hole are available via the "Optional Patch" button at the bottom of the patch program interface.  The files are quite large (about 9MB total), so if the download is going slowly, you may want to postpone downloading the files until later.<BR><BR><BR><BR>As mentioned above, The Hole is a high-level dungeon, designed to support characters starting at about level 40.  It should be regarded as extremely dangerous.  As a note, jumping in The Hole from Paineel is NO LONGER A SHORTCUT TO TOXXULIA FOREST.  The GMs will not recover corpses for people who fall, or jump, or attempt to levitate into The Hole. 
							<br>
							 - Ganza<BR><BR>
							</p>
							
