						<p class="pDate">Wednesday, November 03, 1999</p>
						<p class="pTitle">War! </p>
							<p class=pText>
							<p><br>From high in the stone hallway of the Tribunal I watched the events which led up to the war.<br>It was firece, and the scales of balance and absolute justice were being tipped.  The Halls of The Six Hammers shook with displeasure from the Tribunal as his mighty followers whom had been slain were called to him.  I was among them.<br>He told us of many things, things which are sealed in my mouth as well as my mind, but this I know, we had to staop the army of the Dark ones any way we could.<br>I found myself in the Karanas not far from Highhold and ran unharmed to the wooden bridge which links the vast lands of East and North Karana.  Upon reaching the bridge I saw many fine warriors and clerics of Tunare.  It was very clear battle was approaching, but it never came.<br>People were killing off the various dark elven army in the area but none were advancing to Highhold.  Immediatly my soul was filled with fury.<br>I shouted at the ones who would not test the gates of Highkeep, trying to build the fire of battle in their hearts....I was successful.  While some did stay behind we ammassed a rather large force at the edge of Highhold.<br>After we made a plan ready, we stormed in.<br>It was fierce.  Four generals stormed us as we entered.  Once all our men were inside the generals fell easily enough.<br>Few were hesitant to found the corner as were there reported 3 elites of Innoruuk's army.<br>We rounded it anyway.<br>We found one elite and set upon him taking him down with some effort and made our way to Highkeep.<br>Upon entereing the gates however we found a powerful Elite among us whom was dropping our casters like flies.<br>The warriors and fighters quickly surrounded him as our casters backed up to cast their violent spells.<br>After about 1/4 our losses the Elite fell at the steps of Highkeep.<br>It was not over...the third, even more powerful than the last emerged.<br>I ran to the front lines and begin fighting as best I could, we would have lost that day had it not been for the reinforcements which came running down the halls of the castle of highkeep.<br>As a army we fought with an awesome might, but again, twas a mighty foe we battled and he felled 1/2 our army.<br>After the commotion settled, we looked around, bodies were everywhere!<br>Just then a shout issued! 4 elites were heading our way!!!<br>The call was made to retreat toward Rivervale with Carson McCabe.  I however was not allowed to go as my god saw it fit to take my soul back into the cold halls of the Six Hammers and thus from there I watched as losses were sustained on both sides, but eventually, the stinking Tier'Dal were driven back.<br>They had done it!!<br>Balance was restored!<br>For Now....<br><br></p>
							<br>
							 - Aanamdar<BR><BR>
							</p>
							
					
						<p class="pDate">Tuesday, November 02, 1999</p>
