						<p class="pTitle">The GM Wedding </p>
							<p class=pText>
							Hideaki server GM to Guide Tierra<BR><BR><BR><BR>The sky had shone brightly as the sun began its set upon the far shores, <BR>dissappearing over the lake. The Priestess of Erollisi Marr had appeared upon <BR>the docs with her long raven tresses cascading off of her flowing scarlet <BR>robes. Before her stood Lord Hideaki Tendo, the Avatar of Erollisi Marr with <BR>his bethrothed, Tierra The Loved. Behind them stood Lady Skyestorm alongside <BR>Lord Tiganos, both respectively best man and maid of honor. Also present twas <BR>Sir Banegrivm as the bearer of rings.<BR><BR><BR><BR>The party stood upon oaken docs that carried out upon the waters with the <BR>processional to entowned. All the masses from far and wide, both of light and <BR>of dark twere gatherd in full regalia for the occasion at hand. Hideaki's <BR>armor glinted brilliantly within the setting sun as the two exchanged vows <BR>that day. The Avatar of Erollisi twas as that legendary figure that had <BR>emerged from tales of old of white knights in gleaming plate who would ride <BR>upon white steads to save a fair maiden in distress. He held the hand of his <BR>love who gazed at him longingly, her eyes aglow like the most beautiful of <BR>Kaladims saphires.<BR><BR><BR><BR>Tierra The Loved stood with her tresses kept beneath the veil of purity in <BR>state. Her matching gown flowed downwards to the ground sweepingly with every <BR>flouring movement. This had been a day she had long awaited. Until this very <BR>moment she had never known of her past that brought her departure from Neriak <BR>and her mark of Erollisi upon her that fated her from her birthright. Nor had <BR>she known her name which translated Teir'Ra meant elven love. All this came <BR>to memory with but a white mist that billowed forth from the priestess <BR>revealing her past.<BR><BR><BR><BR>Hideaki took his loves hand as the vows continued onwards. Both lost within <BR>the depths of Erollisi's gift upon them for upon this day they were two fated <BR>from destiny onwards. The vows ended as the rings were placed upon fingers. <BR>The priestess smiles as she spoke her final words "I know pronounce you <BR>husband and wife, you may kiss the bride". Nervously the Avatar of Love drew <BR>his brides veil from her face and embraced her in a kiss that spoke a <BR>thousand words.<BR><BR><BR><BR>It was upon this day many stood to give honor to two who often walked the <BR>lands to aid those without a simple thanks. A time when many came to honor <BR>true love in its most pure and holy form. This would be a time that would <BR>embark upon beginning glories in Norrath. A time when one house would stand <BR>united in Norrath in the pursuits of the gods upon high...enter the House of <BR>Tendo, for upon that day Hideaki and Tierra would remain as one...ascent into <BR>hereafter.<BR><BR> <BR><BR><BR>my gift to the wedded:<BR><BR><BR><BR>"the Call of Love"<BR><BR><BR><BR>Tis spake once upon a merried moon,<BR><BR> hence mine lost love borne.<BR><BR>I prayed for all but mercy,<BR><BR> unto the coming o' that morn.<BR><BR>I watched her gentle mercy,<BR><BR> each time she draweth near.<BR><BR>Therein her sight I felt her touch,<BR><BR> and cried out yet none didst hear.<BR><BR>Upon the field she sat and watched the rose,<BR><BR> as it breathed life into its bloom.<BR><BR>She picted his embrace of love,<BR><BR> whence she befell his gallant grace.<BR><BR>Bestowed twas she to such tender mercies,<BR><BR> whence his arm did take past tears.<BR><BR>For upon one fatefull eve <BR>those prayers came true,<BR><BR> the call of love,<BR><BR>  sweet bliss didst come endeared.<BR><BR><BR><BR><BR>Author - Sir Banegrivm <BR>Blackheart<BR>
							<br>
							 - Aanamdar<BR><BR>
							</p>
							
					
						<p class="pDate">Monday, November 01, 1999</p>
						<p class="pTitle">Given up </p>
							<p class=pText>
							<BR><br>Just wanted to let you guys know that I gave my account up to a friend of mine. I am no longer playing. Plain and simple I believe that Verant took way too long to implement things to keep the higher levels NOT bored. It was starting to feel like a job trying to find something to even fight without some arguement from someone else. I may start another character, but as of right now I don't think so. I will try to continue to update the page with news and server events, but would appreciate any help that you are willing to give. <BR> <BR><br>Long Live Solusek Ro!<BR><br>Retired - Aanamdar.<br><BR><br><BR><br>This does not mean that the page is going down, it just means I retired my account to a friend. =)<br>
							<br>
							 - Aanamdar<BR><BR>
							</p>
							
					
						<p class="pDate">Tuesday, October 26, 1999</p>
						<p class="pTitle">Gnome Stock 99 </p>
							<p class=pText>
							From RotGut:<br><p><br>Welcome to Gnomestock '99 <br>The purpose of this event is to celebrate the discovery of the Third Book of Gimbleston. This book contains many useful and new tinkering formulas, as well as some more words of wisdom from Gimbleston himself. While the location of the book is still only known to a few, those few have been generous enough to share its contents with all gnomes. This act of sharing shows true gnome spirit. I and many others are forever indebted and grateful to this person. <br><br><BR><BR>Some events at Gnomestock '99 will include: <br><BR><BR><br><BR>- Fishing with collapsable fishing poles and animated bait.<br><BR>- A small fireworks display. (snicker)<br><BR>- Free beer and booze for all.<br><BR>- High Diving at the great wheel.<br><BR>- And just some general, 'Gnomeing about'. <br><BR>So come on out and meet everyone! I want to see Ak'anon packed with gnomes, its our heritage, and I hope to see everyone there. <br><BR>Time: This Wedensday, Oct. 27 at 7:00 pm e.s.t. <br><BR>Server: Solusek Ro <br><BR>Place: Ak'anon <br><BR><BR><br>Hope to see you there!<br>Rotgut </p><br><br>
							<br>
							 - Aanamdar<BR><BR>
							</p>
							
					
						<p class="pDate">Monday, October 25, 1999</p>
						<p class="pTitle">Long Time No Update </p>
							<p class=pText>
							Sorry there hasn't been any updates lately, I have been real busy IRL, starting a new job soon. Hopefully soon I can settle down and play my character again. If anyone is interested in keeping up with the news on the page let me know. <BR><br>Good Hunting, and see you soon!<br><br><BR><BR>
							<br>
							 - Aanamdar<BR><BR>
							</p>
							
					
						<p class="pDate">Monday, October 18, 1999</p>
						<p class="pTitle">A Memory </p>
							<p class=pText>
							In memory of Deen Quickheal<br><p><br>>From his name, <br><br>I can gather,<br><br>He was one of pure devotion.<br><p><br>When a friend was low on life.<br>He was quickly there.<br><br>gladly laying his life, <br>For that of a friend.<br><p><br>I'm sure he brought joy to all the lives,<br><br>He touched as he went through our world.<br><br>Cheering a friend up when down,<br> <br>or giving a boost to a young fighter.<br><p><br>I know his family will miss him.<br><br>I know his friends will too,<br>And I'm sure if I knew him, I would cry a tear.<br><p><br>Deen Quickheal, I'm sure, a friend to all<br><br>Will be missed in our world, <br>As well as the one beyond.<br><p><br>A poem by Bollun Rogue of Rivervale and a Knight of Justice<br><BR><br>In Memory of the Man behind Deen Quickheal.<br><p><br>I did not know him, and now I wish I had. Hearing that someone who shares the same world as you for part of our day is no longer going to be here is a sad sad thing to conceive. For those of you who don't know Deen Quickfinger has passed away in the Real World, and shall no longer grace us with his prescence. <br><p><br>As an officer of the Knights of Justice, I speak for my guildmates when I say to the Scarlet Horizon that we are there to talk to if you want and mourn the loss of your Brother.<br><p><br>May the Man Behind Deen Quickheal be going to the Heaven he wanted, and to his family in the real world, Please know that we shall all miss his prescence and send out our condolences.<br><br><br><br><br><br><br><br>
							<br>
							 - Aanamdar<BR><BR>
							</p>
							
					
						<p class="pDate">Thursday, October 14, 1999</p>
						<p class="pTitle">Druid Quests Continued </p>
							<p class=pText>
							Here is some more info about the weapon quests for druids.<br><BR><br><p><br>They start at the Unkempt Druid circle in Rathe Moutnains. You need to talk to Solvedi Aldeberan, he will respond with <p>'Hail, forestwalker. Welcome to the Rathe bear preserve of the Unkempt Druids. We strive to protect nature with diligence and punish her [defilers] with prejudice! <BR> <br><p><br>'There are many defilers of nature about that warrant eradication. Groi Gutblade is a loathsome troll poacher who lurks in South Karana. Slay him and bring me his Lionhide Backpack. Timbur the Tiny takes pride in crushing the trees in North Karana into pulp under his feet. Make him pay for this affront and bring me his Laceless Sandal as proof of his demise. I will give you my own blade if you succeed'</P><br><BR>This quest will get you Solvedi Scimitar, Stats 6/22.<BR><br><br><BR>The other quest there is given by Tibrinn Ember. Here is the dialog:<BR><p><br>'I am Tibrinn Ember, forest friend and Unkempt Druid. Aid us in our [conflict] against the polluters of nature and I will reward you.'<BR><br><BR><br>'Grazhak the Berzerker is a powerful orc who roams these mountains. Slay him and bring me his Mithril Plated Girth. The gorge tyrant himself, King Xorbb, has plagued my halfling brothers for ages. Dispatch this beast and bring me his Slime Crystal Staff as proof of your deed. After you have brought me these items I will give you a weapon as reward for your feats.'<br></P><br><BR><BR> I don't know what the weapon is for this quest just yet, if anyone does let me know please. =)<br><BR><br>
							<br>
							 - Aanamdar<BR><BR>
							</p>
							
